.TH STOP\-MU2EDAQ\-DOWNTIME\-LOGGER.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh \- stop the downtime logger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
The script reads
.I mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.pid
from its own directory, sends
.B SIGTERM
to that PID, polls once a second for up to
.B \-\-timeout
seconds, and sends
.B SIGKILL
if the process is still alive.
It then removes the PID file and deletes the directory
.I /tmp/daq\-test
(the fixture directory of
.IR config/local.yaml )
if it exists, whatever configuration the application was running.
The
.B \-\-force
path and the nothing\-to\-stop paths skip that deletion.
.PP
A missing PID file, or one naming a dead process, is reported and the
script exits 0 (removing the stale file).
.PP
.B SIGTERM is not a clean shutdown for this application.
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1)
installs a handler only for
.BR SIGINT ;
on
.B SIGTERM
the Python process exits at once (status 143) without running its Qt
.I aboutToQuit
cleanup.
A downtime event open at that moment keeps
.B ended_at
NULL in the database, is not reattached on the next start, cannot be ended
with
.IR "End downtime now" ,
and is counted as ongoing downtime by every later
.B /report
range.
Close such an event by editing it (clear
.IR Ongoing ,
set the end time, Save).
To stop cleanly, quit from the tray menu or send
.B SIGINT
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Seconds to wait after
.B SIGTERM
before escalating to
.BR SIGKILL .
Default
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Send
.B SIGKILL
immediately.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.pid
PID file written by
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1).
.TP
.I /tmp/daq\-test
Removed recursively after every
.BR SIGTERM / SIGKILL
stop.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The process was stopped, or there was nothing to stop.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown option or an option missing its argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stop with a 30\-second grace period:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh \-\-timeout 30
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop cleanly without the
.B SIGTERM
path, closing any open event first:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kill \-INT "$(cat mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.pid)"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman and the Mu2e DAQ group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
